          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "里 (lǐ) is inherited from Middle Chinese liX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'inside' and, through an older book, 'the inside of a garment'."
            }
